# Plane Radar

Firmware for **ESP32-C3 Super Mini** + **GC9A01** round display (240×240). Live ADS-B radar around a configured location.

## Layer map

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Config | `include/config.h` | Pins, timings, defaults, portal names |
| Hardware | `include/hardware/`, `src/hardware/` | LovyanGFX display, embedded VLW font |
| Services | `include/services/`, `src/services/` | WiFi, location, ADS-B fetch |
| UI | `include/ui/`, `src/ui/` | Radar grid, aircraft, runways, status screens |
| Data | `include/data/`, `src/data/` | Generated airport/runway dataset |
| Entry | `src/main.cpp` | Boot flow and main loop |

## Namespaces

- `config::` — compile-time constants
- `services::adsb`, `services::location` — network and persisted location
- `ui::radar`, `ui::runway` — display logic
- `data::large_airports` — embedded runway data

## Constraints

- **PlatformIO env**: `supermini` only (Arduino + espressif32@6.5.0)
- **No OTA slot** — single ~3 MB app partition (`partitions/plane_radar.csv`)
- **Display stack**: LovyanGFX via `lgfx_config.hpp` — do not introduce TFT_eSPI or alternate drivers
- **README is the user spec** — keep behavior and docs aligned when changing features

## Change discipline

- Minimize scope; match existing C++17 Arduino style and file layout
- Put tunables in `config.h`, layout constants in `ui/radar_theme.h`, range presets in `ui/radar_range.h`
- Do not hand-edit generated `src/data/large_airports_data.cpp`
